RULES:
- 6-10 plays for 1st & 10 (the biggest bucket)
- 3-5 plays for each other situation
- 2-3 blitz beaters minimum — these are critical
- At least 1 shot play and 1 gadget play
- Use a mix of Run, Pass, RPO, Screen, Play Action
- Vary personnel groupings (don't stay in 11 personnel every play)
- Confidence 1-5: 5 = absolute money against this opponent, 1 = emergency option
- Reference specific tendencies from the report when explaining why plays work
- If existing plays from the playbook fit, USE THEM. Build on what we already have.
- Be creative with play names — these should sound like real play calls`;

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// OPENING SCRIPT PROMPT
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

export const OPENING_SCRIPT_PROMPT = `Build the first 15 plays we will script for the opening of the game. This is the opening drive strategy.

OPPONENT TENDENCY DATA:
{tendencyData}

OUR GAME PLAN:
{gamePlanData}

Generate the opening script as valid JSON:
{
  "script": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "play_name": "Play name",
      "formation": "Offensive formation",
      "play_type": "Run|Pass|RPO|Screen|Play Action",
      "personnel": "11|12|21",
      "strategic_reason": "Why this play is in this slot. Reference opponent tendencies."
    }
  ],
  "philosophy": "2-3 sentence summary of the opening drive philosophy — what are we trying to accomplish in the first 15 plays?"
}

OPENING SCRIPT PRINCIPLES:
1. Play 1 should establish our identity — show the defense who we are
2. Feature our best playmaker within the first 3 plays
3. Include at least one shot play (deep) in the first 10 plays
4. Mix run and pass to prevent tendencies from forming
5. Use at least 2 different personnel groupings
6. Include 1 play specifically designed to gather intelligence (diagnose coverage)
7. Build in a constraint play (counter/bootleg off a look we've already shown)
8. Have answers ready for 2nd-and-long and 3rd-and-medium within the script
9. Don't get cute early — run what we do best
10. End the script with a high-confidence play for 3rd down conversion`;

